description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/docs-decision-answer-scan.ts. TWO string replacements in that ONE file. Change nothing else.

An empty-string env var defeats the `??` default. This container exports some endpoint variables as EMPTY STRINGS, and `??` falls back only on null/undefined — never on "". So `process.env["STATEFUL_UI_VESSEL_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8270"` yields "" and the fetch below is issued against an empty endpoint instead of the intended default. The repo already has the fix helper: `env(key, fallback)` in src/config.ts treats an empty/whitespace-only value as absent. This file already imports from ../config.js, so only the import list needs widening.

EDIT 1 — replace this exact existing line:

import { DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT, METABOB_API_KEY } from "../config.js";

with:

import { DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT, METABOB_API_KEY, env } from "../config.js";

EDIT 2 — replace these exact existing two lines:

            const uiEndpoint =
              process.env["STATEFUL_UI_VESSEL_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8270";

with:

            const uiEndpoint = env("STATEFUL_UI_VESSEL_ENDPOINT", "http://127.0.0.1:8270");

Do not touch METABOB_API_KEY or any other env read: an API key is not an endpoint, and an empty key is a legitimate "no credential".

The change must typecheck (bun run lint). VERIFY BY CONSEQUENCE: with STATEFUL_UI_VESSEL_ENDPOINT exported as the empty string, `uiEndpoint` is "http://127.0.0.1:8270" rather than "", so the feedback POST goes to the stateful-ui vessel instead of to a relative path.

